# Kinetum Runtime @KINETUM_VERSION@

Runtime artifacts for the Kinetum Platform.

## Installation

The versioned release page supplies a complete command for each architecture.
Choose the x86-64 or AArch64 runtime entry explicitly. In this x86-64 example,
`RELEASE_URL` denotes the versioned HTTPS asset directory from that page:

```bash
set -o pipefail
curl -fsSL "$RELEASE_URL/kinetum-runtime-@KINETUM_VERSION@-x86_64.install.sh" | sudo /bin/sh
```

The AArch64 entry is `kinetum-runtime-@KINETUM_VERSION@-aarch64.install.sh`.
Each entry is bound to one archive and rejects a different host architecture.
It verifies the archive against the entry's embedded SHA-256 and invokes the native
installer carried by that archive. There is no
manual checksum or unpacking step. Ubuntu 24.04 and its runtime libraries are
required; online setup installs those libraries through APT.

Public-release CPU requirements are the Core i7/Nehalem instruction-set
baseline on x86-64 and Armv8-A with CRC on AArch64. A locally built native
package may require additional features of its build machine. The architecture
check and integrity verification do not convert those compiled requirements.

The same `.install.sh` is produced for a locally built package. To install
local files, including on an offline host, place it beside its matching
`.tar.gz`. With the system prerequisites already installed, run from that
directory on x86-64:

```bash
sudo /bin/sh ./kinetum-runtime-@KINETUM_VERSION@-x86_64.install.sh --offline-directory "$PWD"
```

This mode skips downloads and APT installation. An installer produced without
a publication URL requires `--offline-directory`; it never invents an address
or chooses a local archive implicitly.

The default prefix is `/opt/kinetum`; `--prefix /absolute/path` selects another
protected prefix. Runtime installation requires root. It verifies the full
payload before replacement, preserves `sdk/` and `dependencies/`, and checks
the installed result. A failed replacement restores prior entries; an
incomplete restoration reports the original failure and recovery state and
retains the recovery tree. Stop services before replacement: installation does not
coordinate a live runtime or start any service. An interrupted runtime
replacement can be unavailable and must be retried before service startup.

Only runtime and SDK are public products. Internal validation kits live outside
the installation prefix. Build-only dependencies remain outside the runtime
payload and are never runtime inputs.

The release channel authenticates delivery. SHA-256 provides integrity under
that channel; it is not a second publisher signature.

## Runtime closure

The package contains the runtime executables, the ACL, NAT44,
and QoS built-in module images, and the exact host and DPDK provider components.
The signed installed-provider inventory authenticates `kinetum_dp` and that
provider closure. The payload manifest defines exact runtime membership and
hashes every other installed runtime artifact, including the inventory,
signature, native-admission receipt, and release metadata. Its own required
path and grammar are verified independently; it does not expand the inventory
signature's trust claim.

`kinetum_pack` creates configuration-and-module deployment bundles. It does not
redistribute runtime executables or provider artifacts.

Apache-2.0 terms and the Kinetum notice are installed at the package root.
Runtime-specific third-party notices are in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`; exact
DPDK license material is under `share/licenses/KinetumDPDK/dpdk/`, and exact
static-closure attribution is in
`share/licenses/KinetumDPDK/DPDK_STATIC_CLOSURE_NOTICE.txt`.

## Verification

```bash
/opt/kinetum/bin/kinetum-info --check
```
